&lt;h1&gt;


  Adding Real‑Time IP Communication Status to the TV Inventory Dashboard
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; I extended the Prisma schema and React UI to surface a boolean “IP Comm” flag for each TV device, letting the inventory table show live connectivity status. The change required a new column, type updates, a badge component, and a small store tweak—all done without breaking existing queries.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our inventory page lists hundreds of TV devices, but we had no way to tell if a TV was currently reachable over the network. The backend periodically ingests a CSV report (&lt;code&gt;sis_report.csv&lt;/code&gt;) that contains a &lt;code&gt;terminalAddress&lt;/code&gt; (MAC) and a boolean &lt;code&gt;ip_comm&lt;/code&gt; indicating whether the TV responded to a ping test. The UI displayed a “—” for that column because the Prisma model &lt;code&gt;TvDevice&lt;/code&gt; didn’t have a matching field, resulting in a runtime error:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;TypeError: Cannot read property 'ipComm' of undefined
    at InventoryTable (src/features/inventory/InventoryTable.tsx:42:27)
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The missing field also meant we couldn’t filter or sort by connectivity status, limiting our ability to quickly isolate offline units.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  What I Tried First
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My first attempt was to compute the IP status on the client side by joining the CSV data with the fetched devices in &lt;code&gt;useDevicesStore&lt;/code&gt;. I added a helper &lt;code&gt;calcIpComm(devices, csvRows)&lt;/code&gt; that returned a map of MAC → boolean. Then I patched each &lt;code&gt;TvDeviceRow&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;ipComm&lt;/code&gt; before rendering.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Problems:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Performance hit&lt;/strong&gt; – The CSV can be &amp;gt;10 k rows; parsing it on every page load caused a noticeable UI lag (&amp;gt;500 ms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Stale data&lt;/strong&gt; – The CSV is refreshed by a separate cron job; the client‑side merge never updated until a full page reload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Type mismatch&lt;/strong&gt; – The &lt;code&gt;TvDeviceRow&lt;/code&gt; interface in &lt;code&gt;use-devices-store.ts&lt;/code&gt; didn’t have an &lt;code&gt;ipComm&lt;/code&gt; field, so TypeScript threw errors across the codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I reverted that approach and decided to push the IP flag into the database so the UI could treat it like any other column.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. Extend the Prisma schema
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;File: &lt;code&gt;prisma/schema.prisma&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -49,6 +49,13 @@&lt;/span&gt; model TvDevice {
   tvPowerOns7Days  Int?
   stateModified    DateTime?
&lt;span class="err"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  // IP communication status – derived from the SIS report (MAC ↔ ip_comm)
+  // Null means we haven’t processed a report for this device yet.
+  ipComm           Boolean?   @default(null)
+  ipCommCheckedAt  DateTime?  @default(null)
&lt;/span&gt; }
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Why Boolean?&lt;/em&gt; The SIS report only tells us “reachable” (&lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt;) or “not reachable” (&lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt;). Using &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; signals “unknown” – useful for newly added TVs that haven’t been scanned yet.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After the schema change I ran:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npx prisma migrate dev &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--name&lt;/span&gt; add-ip-comm-status
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Prisma generated the migration SQL:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight sql"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;ALTER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;TABLE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"TvDevice"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;ADD&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;COLUMN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"ipComm"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;BOOLEAN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;ALTER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;TABLE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"TvDevice"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;ADD&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;COLUMN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"ipCommCheckedAt"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;TIMESTAMP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  2. Update the TypeScript store
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;File: &lt;code&gt;src/hooks/use-devices-store.ts&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -21,6 +21,8 @@&lt;/span&gt; export interface TvDeviceRow {
   chromecastState: string | null;
   stays60Days: number | null;
   tvPowerOns7Days: number | null;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  ipComm: boolean | null;
+  ipCommCheckedAt: string | null;
&lt;/span&gt; }
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The store pulls rows via &lt;code&gt;prisma.tvDevice.findMany()&lt;/code&gt;. Adding the fields required no extra code because Prisma automatically includes them in the generated type.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  3. Create a badge component for IP status
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;File: &lt;code&gt;src/components/inventory/status-badge.tsx&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;IpCommBadge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;variant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"neutral"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;—&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;variant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"success"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Online&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;variant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"danger"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Offline&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I kept the UI consistent with existing badges (&lt;code&gt;OccupiedBadge&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;OutOfServiceBadge&lt;/code&gt;). The component returns a neutral dash for unknown status, mirroring the rest of the table.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  4. Wire the badge into the inventory table
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;File: &lt;code&gt;src/features/inventory/InventoryTable.tsx&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@&lt;/span&gt; import {
   SerialBadge,
   OutOfServiceBadge,
   OccupiedBadge,
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  IpCommBadge,
&lt;/span&gt; } from "@/components/inventory/status-badge";
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then inside the row rendering loop:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;td&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"px-4 py-2"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;IpCommBadge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;row&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;td&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I also added a column header:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;th&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"px-4 py-2 text-left"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;IP Comm&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;th&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  5. Populate the new columns from the SIS report
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The backend job that processes &lt;code&gt;sis_report.csv&lt;/code&gt; already runs nightly. I extended its parser (&lt;code&gt;src/jobs/process-sis-report.ts&lt;/code&gt;) to upsert the &lt;code&gt;ipComm&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ipCommCheckedAt&lt;/code&gt; fields:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tvDevice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;upsert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;terminalAddress&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;mac&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ipCommFlag&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;ipCommCheckedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;terminalAddress&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;mac&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// other required fields...&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ipCommFlag&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;ipCommCheckedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Because the fields are optional, existing rows are updated without a migration lock, and newly discovered devices receive the flag immediately.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  6. Adjust the API response shape
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our GraphQL resolver (&lt;code&gt;src/graphql/resolvers/tvDevice.ts&lt;/code&gt;) now includes &lt;code&gt;ipComm&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ipCommCheckedAt&lt;/code&gt; in the selection set:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tvDevice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;findMany&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;ipCommCheckedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// …other fields&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;No client‑side changes were needed beyond the badge import.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Key Takeaway
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Never treat a missing column as a UI‑only problem; push the data into the source of truth.&lt;/strong&gt; Adding a boolean flag to the Prisma model gave us a single source of truth, eliminated client‑side merging, and let us reuse existing type‑generation pipelines. The pattern—extend the schema, run a migration, update the store interface, and add a small UI component—scales cleanly for any new telemetry field.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  What's Next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I plan to add a &lt;strong&gt;real‑time WebSocket&lt;/strong&gt; subscription that pushes &lt;code&gt;ipComm&lt;/code&gt; updates as soon as the SIS job finishes, so the badge flips from “—” to “Online/Offline” without a page refresh. This will involve:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adding a &lt;code&gt;pubsub.publish('IP_COMM_UPDATED', device)&lt;/code&gt; call in the job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposing a GraphQL subscription resolver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Updating &lt;code&gt;InventoryTable&lt;/code&gt; to listen via &lt;code&gt;useSubscription&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That will close the loop between data ingestion and UI responsiveness.&lt;/p&gt;




